# Which of OpenGamingCollective's ~153 patches we take, as extended regexes
# matched against the patch name with its leading number stripped.
#
# WHY NOT NUMERIC RANGES. The arch-arm64 package used OGC_RANGES="0006 0028-0060".
# That is safe only within one mainline base: when OGC rebases onto a new kernel,
# patches that landed upstream are dropped and everything after them renumbers,
# so a fixed range silently selects a different, wrong set. Names are stable
# across a rebase because they are derived from the commit subject.
#
# Verified at v7.2.1-ogc3: these three lines select exactly the 34 patches that
# "0006 0028-0060" selected -- 32 sched-*, one stop_machine, one usbhid.
#
# See also patches/ogc.select.deny and the contiguity guard in fetch-patches.sh,
# which fails the build if an unselected patch appears *inside* the numeric span
# of what we did select. That guard is the real protection: a regex cannot know
# that a new mm/ patch was inserted as a dependency of the scheduler series.

# The scheduler block, in full: Zijlstra's EEVDF single-runqueue rework plus the
# load-balancer and topology series that follows it.
#
# Taken whole, deliberately. It is contiguous, it is what OGC tests as a unit,
# and its internal Fixes: edges make subsets actively wrong:
#
#   "sched/fair: Fix flat hierarchy"      Fixes: "sched/eevdf: Move to a single
#                                         runqueue" -- so the tempting cut before
#                                         the load-balancer work ships the rework
#                                         without its fix.
#   "sched/eevdf: Delayed dequeue ..."    Fixes: "sched/eevdf: Cancel slice
#                                         protection if short..."
#
# Patches that read as x86-only are NOT dropped. The SMT ones compile in because
# CONFIG_SCHED_SMT=y in our config; they are simply no-ops on a topology that
# reports no SMT siblings. Carrying them costs a few unreachable branches;
# cutting them costs a rebase decision on every -ogcN bump. Conversely the
# asymmetric-capacity and misfit work matters *more* on SM8750 big.LITTLE than
# on OGC's own x86 targets.
^FROM-ML-sched-
^FROM-ML-stop_machine-

# HID: usbhid: skip interrupt IN polling for devices with no input reports.
# Generic despite the ASUS ROG framing -- there is no VID/PID match in it. Any
# composite device with an input-less interface drops reports on its sibling
# interface once something opens the hidraw node, and Steam Input opens every
# hidraw node it finds.
^FROM-ML-HID-usbhid-skip-interrupt-IN-polling
